# WorldForge v1.6x headless batch scratch (regenerated by --prepare)
procedural/generated/runtime/_prepare_maps.json
procedural/generated/runtime/_ground_prepare_maps.json

# v1.8 CombatForge — UE transients / crash logs / local save-slot junk.
# APPEND-ONLY addendum: Saved/, Intermediate/, DerivedDataCache/, *.log and *.tmp
# are already ignored above; these cover the remaining local-runtime junk a combat
# playtest can drop (save slots + crash dumps/context) so it never gets staged.
*.sav
*.dmp
*.mdmp
*-Crash.log
*.runtime-xml
Saved/Crashes/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local engine/plugin environment noise
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Third-party engine plugins may be installed locally for development,
# but are not part of the WorldForge source payload unless explicitly
# added by a dedicated feature PR with validation gates.
#
# v2.5 addendum — EXCEPTION, deliberate and gated: `Plugins/5.8/` (Houdini
# Engine / Niagara / LiveLink, H21.0.753 builds for UE 5.8) IS tracked. The
# UE 5.8 uproject marks HoudiniNiagara required (not Optional), so a clean
# checkout must carry the plugin source or the project will not load. Only
# Source/Content/Config/Resources are tracked; `Plugins/**/Binaries/` and
# `Plugins/**/Intermediate/` above still exclude ~190MB of build output, which
# UE regenerates. NOTE: Houdini Engine additionally requires a local Houdini
# install (HAPI) at runtime — the tracked payload alone is not self-contained.
# Covered by the v2.5 capability manifest. The 5.7-era paths below stay ignored.
Plugins/HoudiniEngine/
Plugins/HoudiniNiagara/
Plugins/HoudiniLiveLink/
Plugins/UELLMToolkit/

# Houdini local/generated transients
Content/HoudiniEngine/Bake/
Content/HoudiniEngine/Temp/
